            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>The invention relates to a polarity changeable fiber optic assembly, comprising:at least two optical fiber segments; andat least two fiber optic connectors (10) connecting the at least two optical fiber segments via an adapter (20) therebetween, each fiber optic connector of the at least two fiber optic connectors including a first polarity key (18A) on one side of a housing of the fiber optic connector and a second polarity key (18B) on an opposite side of the housing (14), each of the two polarity keys movable within a passageway (22) between a first active position and a second retracted position without disassembly of the at least two fiber optic connectors,wherein the at least two optical fiber segments are presented in a first polarity configuration when the first polarity key (18A) is in the first active position and the second polarity key (18B) is in the second retracted position, andwherein the first polarity configuration is changed to a second polarity configuration when the first polarity key is moved to the second retracted position and the second polarity key is moved to the first active position without disassembly of the at least two fiber optic connectors.</p>
            </abstract>
